    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-intro",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Authoring switches",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 320
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 620,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Authoring switches\n\nWhat a person, a template or an agent can set on a node or a graph to change how it looks or behaves, in one place.\n\n**One description, many readers.** Each switch below is a node, and the node carries its own description as data (`data.switch`: name, scope, where it is written, value type, default, the values it takes, effect, the modes it applies in). The card on each node is generated from that data, so there is one description and the page is not a second copy. The Properties panel, a template or an agent can read the same fields.\n\n**Policies are nodes too** (`data.policy`). A switch names the policy that governs it (`governedBy`) or the one it overrides (`overrides`) by the policy's id, in place of edges until there is an edge class for them.\n\n**How the pieces fit.** The script API is generic (`updateNode`, `updateView`, `createNode`, `applyDeltas`), so any switch can be written by a Method that declares the effect that allows it. This page says what can be written and where; the API says how.\n\n**Checked.** Each row was read against the code. A \"none found\" under Panel means no control turned up, not that none exists."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-policy-visibility",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Visibility",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": 320
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 480,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Visibility (policy)\n\n## Visibility is three questions\n\n1. **Does the node exist?** It is in the graph, or it is not.\n2. **Is it eligible in this mode?** The *type rule* answers: a root, face, glyph, import, export or method is plumbing, and plumbing is for editing. `showInBrowse: true` is the one override of this rule.\n3. **Is it shown?** `visible` answers: false hides it, true is the default and changes nothing.\n\n`visibilityRole` is an older way to say (2) and cannot override the rule; it is kept for Scripts that present a node.web surface."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "policy": {
          "id": "policy-visibility",
          "name": "Visibility",
          "reads": [
            "visible",
            "show-in-browse",
            "visibility-role"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-policy-root-handle",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "The root handle",
      "position": {
        "x": 1900,
        "y": 320
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 480,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# The root handle (policy)\n\n## The root handle\n\nThe root Port always exists. Whether its handle is drawn is a policy: **auto** draws it when the graph is open, pointed at, or a connection is being made; `root.handle` can force it on (`shown`) or off (`hidden`). The Port and its Handle are separate: hiding one does not remove the other."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "policy": {
          "id": "policy-root-handle",
          "name": "The root handle",
          "reads": [
            "root-handle",
            "default-handle"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-policy-which-view",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Which view shows",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": 840
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 480,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Which view shows (policy)\n\n## Which view shows\n\n`semanticLevel` and `semanticZoom.resolution` describe a face. Which face a tile shows at a given size is the app's policy: by how large the graph is drawn (glyph, then summary, then detail), and for a node, by the camera's zoom. The thresholds are in `semanticPresentation.js` and `graphViewPresentation.js`; they are not switches."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "policy": {
          "id": "policy-which-view",
          "name": "Which view shows",
          "reads": [
            "semantic-level",
            "semantic-zoom-resolution"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-policy-edge-class",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Edge class",
      "position": {
        "x": 1900,
        "y": 840
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 480,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Edge class (policy)\n\n## What the class decides\n\nAn edge's `type` is its class, and the class is not a switch: it supplies the style an edge wears when it names none. The edge's own `style` wins over the class, and the class wins over the graph's default edge colour. Routing and bundling, how lines are grouped and where they meet a border, are the app's policy and are not switches."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "policy": {
          "id": "policy-edge-class",
          "name": "Edge class",
          "reads": [
            "edge-color",
            "edge-width",
            "edge-dash",
            "edge-route",
            "edge-opacity",
            "edge-show-arrow",
            "edge-arrow-size",
            "edge-arrow-position",
            "edge-animation",
            "edge-animation-speed",
            "edge-glow",
            "edge-gradient",
            "edge-strokes"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-switch-visible",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "visible",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1400
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 640,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## visible\n\nFalse hides the node while browsing; editing always shows it. True never brings plumbing back: the type rule answers that, and showInBrowse overrides it.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node, applies to any |\n| Written at | `node.visible` |\n| Type | boolean |\n| Default | true |\n| Valid | true, false |\n| Applies | browse |\n| Properties panel | no, drawn from the contract in Presentation |\n| Written down | AGENTS.md |\n| Status | built |\n| Governed by | policy-visibility |"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "switch": {
          "id": "visible",
          "name": "visible",
          "scope": "node",
          "writePath": "node.visible",
          "valueType": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "effect": "False hides the node while browsing; editing always shows it. True never brings plumbing back: the type rule answers that, and showInBrowse overrides it.",
          "modes": [
            "browse"
          ],
          "panel": "no, drawn from the contract in Presentation",
          "writtenDown": "AGENTS.md",
          "status": "built",
          "governedBy": "policy-visibility",
          "appliesTo": [
            "any"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-switch-show-in-browse",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "showInBrowse",
      "position": {
        "x": 640,
        "y": 1400
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 640,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## showInBrowse\n\nBrings a root, face, glyph, import, export or method into browse mode, as on a primitive page whose subject is the root and the views. visible: false still hides it.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node, applies to any |\n| Written at | `node.data.showInBrowse` |\n| Type | boolean |\n| Default | false |\n| Valid | true |\n| Applies | browse |\n| Properties panel | no |\n| Written down | AGENTS.md, this page |\n| Status | built, one page first |\n| Overrides | policy-visibility |"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "switch": {
          "id": "show-in-browse",
          "name": "showInBrowse",
          "scope": "node",
          "writePath": "node.data.showInBrowse",
          "valueType": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "enum": [
            true
          ],
          "effect": "Brings a root, face, glyph, import, export or method into browse mode, as on a primitive page whose subject is the root and the views. visible: false still hides it.",
          "modes": [
            "browse"
          ],
          "panel": "no",
          "writtenDown": "AGENTS.md, this page",
          "status": "built, one page first",
          "overrides": "policy-visibility",
          "appliesTo": [
            "any"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-switch-visibility-role",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "visibilityRole",
      "position": {
        "x": 1280,
        "y": 1400
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 640,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## visibilityRole\n\nNames a node as plumbing or as content. Ignored for the types the rule hides; honoured only for a Script that names a node.web presentation. Do not use it to show a root or a face.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node, applies to any |\n| Written at | `node.data.visibilityRole` |\n| Type | enum |\n| Default | by the node's type |\n| Valid | editor, browser |\n| Applies | browse |\n| Properties panel | no |\n| Written down | AGENTS.md, as a warning |\n| Status | built |\n| Governed by | policy-visibility |"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "switch": {
          "id": "visibility-role",
          "name": "visibilityRole",
          "scope": "node",
          "writePath": "node.data.visibilityRole",
          "valueType": "enum",
          "default": "by the node's type",
          "enum": [
            "editor",
            "browser"
          ],
          "effect": "Names a node as plumbing or as content. Ignored for the types the rule hides; honoured only for a Script that names a node.web presentation. Do not use it to show a root or a face.",
          "modes": [
            "browse"
          ],
          "panel": "no",
          "writtenDown": "AGENTS.md, as a warning",
          "status": "built",
          "governedBy": "policy-visibility",
          "appliesTo": [
            "any"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-switch-position-locked",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "positionLocked",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 2080
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 640,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## positionLocked\n\nPins the node. A pinned ground is drawn in a layer of its own beneath every other node and is never stepped down to a smaller view.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node, applies to any |\n| Written at | `node.positionLocked` |\n| Type | boolean |\n| Default | false |\n| Valid | true, false |\n| Applies | edit, browse |\n| Properties panel | lock toggle in the editor |\n| Written down | AGENTS.md (ground) |\n| Status | built |"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "switch": {
          "id": "position-locked",
          "name": "positionLocked",
          "scope": "node",
          "writePath": "node.positionLocked",
          "valueType": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "effect": "Pins the node. A pinned ground is drawn in a layer of its own beneath every other node and is never stepped down to a smaller view.",
          "modes": [
            "edit",
            "browse"
          ],
          "panel": "lock toggle in the editor",
          "writtenDown": "AGENTS.md (ground)",
          "status": "built",
          "appliesTo": [
            "any"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-switch-show-label",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "showLabel",
      "position": {
        "x": 640,
        "y": 2080
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 640,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## showLabel\n\nWhether the node draws its label. False leaves the label text out of the title bar (the bar stays: it is the node's drag handle and holds its actions) and out of a content node's summary.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node, applies to any |\n| Written at | `node.showLabel` |\n| Type | boolean |\n| Default | true |\n| Valid | true, false |\n| Applies | edit, browse |\n| Properties panel | none found |\n| Written down | no |\n| Status | built |"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "switch": {
          "id": "show-label",
          "name": "showLabel",
          "scope": "node",
          "writePath": "node.showLabel",
          "valueType": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "effect": "Whether the node draws its label. False leaves the label text out of the title bar (the bar stays: it is the node's drag handle and holds its actions) and out of a content node's summary.",
          "modes": [
            "edit",
            "browse"
          ],
          "panel": "none found",
          "writtenDown": "no",
          "status": "built",
          "appliesTo": [
            "any"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-switch-hide-label",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "hideLabel",
      "position": {
        "x": 1280,
        "y": 2080
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 640,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## hideLabel\n\nThe port's name is never shown as a sign. Set on the root and out-bottom ports.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | handle, applies to port |\n| Written at | `port.metadata.hideLabel` |\n| Type | boolean |\n| Default | false |\n| Valid | true |\n| Applies | edit |\n| Properties panel | no |\n| Written down | no |\n| Status | built |"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "switch": {
          "id": "hide-label",
          "name": "hideLabel",
          "scope": "handle",
          "writePath": "port.metadata.hideLabel",
          "valueType": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "enum": [
            true
          ],
          "effect": "The port's name is never shown as a sign. Set on the root and out-bottom ports.",
          "modes": [
            "edit"
          ],
          "panel": "no",
          "writtenDown": "no",
          "status": "built",
          "appliesTo": [
            "port"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-switch-rotation",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "rotation",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 2760
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 640,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## rotation\n\nTurns the node. Its handles and the edges that end on it turn with it.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node, applies to any |\n| Written at | `node.data.rotation` |\n| Type | number (degrees, clockwise) |\n| Default | 0 |\n| Valid | any |\n| Applies | edit, browse |\n| Properties panel | none found |\n| Written down | docs, in part |\n| Status | built |"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "switch": {
          "id": "rotation",
          "name": "rotation",
          "scope": "node",
          "writePath": "node.data.rotation",
          "valueType": "number",
          "unit": "degrees, clockwise",
          "default": 0,
          "effect": "Turns the node. Its handles and the edges that end on it turn with it.",
          "modes": [
            "edit",
            "browse"
          ],
          "panel": "none found",
          "writtenDown": "docs, in part",
          "status": "built",
          "appliesTo": [
            "any"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-switch-semantic-zoom-resolution",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "semanticZoom.resolution",
      "position": {
        "x": 640,
        "y": 2760
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 640,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## semanticZoom.resolution\n\nWhere along the zoom a view takes over: 1 is the conventional detail, lower is smaller, and 3 opens the whole graph. Fractional values allow any number of views.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node, applies to face |\n| Written at | `node.data.semanticZoom.resolution` |\n| Type | number |\n| Default | 1 |\n| Valid | 0 to 2.99 |\n| Applies | browse |\n| Properties panel | yes (\"Resolution\") |\n| Written down | the panel's helper text only |\n| Status | built |\n| Governed by | policy-which-view |"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "switch": {
          "id": "semantic-zoom-resolution",
          "name": "semanticZoom.resolution",
          "scope": "node",
          "writePath": "node.data.semanticZoom.resolution",
          "valueType": "number",
          "default": 1,
          "range": [
            0,
            2.99
          ],
          "effect": "Where along the zoom a view takes over: 1 is the conventional detail, lower is smaller, and 3 opens the whole graph. Fractional values allow any number of views.",
          "modes": [
            "browse"
          ],
          "panel": "yes (\"Resolution\")",
          "writtenDown": "the panel's helper text only",
          "status": "built",
          "governedBy": "policy-which-view",
          "appliesTo": [
            "face"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-contract-switches-switch-semantic-level",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "semanticLevel",
      "position": {
        "x": 1280,
        "y": 2760
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 640,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## semanticLevel\n\nNames the representation a face is. Which one shows at a size is a policy.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node, applies to face |\n| Written at | `node.data.semanticLevel` (also read at `node.data.view.semanticLevel`) |\n| Type | enum |\n| Default | detail |\n| Valid | badge, icon, summary, detail; also read: glyph as badge, dot as badge, card as summary |\n| Applies | browse |\n| Properties panel | no |\n| Written down | no |\n| Status | built |\n| Governed by | policy-which-view |"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-switches"
        },
        "switch": {
          "id": "semantic-level",
          "name": "semanticLevel",
          "scope": "node",
          "writePath": "node.data.semanticLevel",
          "alsoRead": "node.data.view.semanticLevel",
          "valueType": "enum",
          "default": "detail",
          "enum": [
            "badge",
            "icon",
            "summary",
            "detail"
          ],
          "aliases": {
            "glyph": "badge",
            "dot": "badge",
            "card": "summary"
          },
          "effect": "Names the representation a face is. Which one shows at a size is a policy.",
          "modes": [
            "browse"
          ],
          "panel": "no",
          "writtenDown": "no",
          "status": "built",
          "governedBy": "policy-which-view",
          "appliesTo": [
            "face"
          ]
        }
      }
